  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">GFI Increasing DRM by Promoting Corporate, Natural Resource and Professional Integrity Ghana</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ghana Integrity Initiative (GII). This will conduct research and the produce policy resources, including a report, policy briefs, a video and factsheets on the gaps in the legislative framework of beneficial ownership as well as the connection between beneficial ownership to IFFs in the real estate sector. GII will seek to engage with private and public sector stakeholders to promote the incorporation of illicit enrichment in Ghana&#x2019;s Criminal Code. GII will also conduct research including a scoping report on the professional standards and Anti Money Londering (AML)  obligations of gatekeepers in Ghana. GII&#x2019;s advocacy efforts will focus on the publication of factsheets to use for advocacy with government, private sector, civil society and journalists, as well as organizing meetings with stakeholders to highlight the role of professional enablers in facilitating IFFs. GII will play a supporting role in the organization of journalist training for a small component of the training on illicit money going into the real estate sector in Ghana.


Capitalizing on Friends of the Nations&#x2019;s (FoN&apos;S) expertise and experience in the extractives sector, their  work will focus on research and advocacy on illicit financial flows in the mining, cacao and fisheries sectors of Ghana. This will include the publication of three reports mapping supply chain issues that limit domestic resource mobilization in each of the three sectors, as well as efforts to engage on natural resource and trade
integrity issues with stakeholders in the private sector, government, media, international organizations
and civil society. Finally, FoN will take the lead on providing journalist training, focusing on education and
investigative techniques to produce analysis of illicit financial flows in connection with the mining, cacao
and fisheries sectors.</narrative>
  </description>
